
# Code Block Tests

## Python with language class

```python
def hello():
    print("Hello, world!")

for i in range(10):
    hello()
```

## JavaScript with language class

```js
function greet(name) {
    return `Hello, ${name}!`;
}
```

## Code block with no language

```
just some plain code
  with indentation preserved
    and more indentation
```

## Bare pre (no code element)

```
This is preformatted text
  without a code wrapper
    just raw pre
```

## Paragraph after code

This paragraph should be separated from the code block above by a blank line.

# Blockquote Tests

## Simple blockquote

> This is a quoted paragraph.

## Multi-paragraph blockquote

> First quoted paragraph.
> 
> Second quoted paragraph with **bold** text.

## Nested blockquote

> Outer quote.
> 
> > Inner quote.

## Blockquote with code

> Here is some code:
> 
> ```python
> x = 42
> ```
